<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jiang Zemin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1926">1926</a>–<a href="/years/2022">2022</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jiang Zemin was a Chinese Communist leader who became general secretary of the party after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/1989-tiananmen-square-protests-and-massacre">Tiananmen Square protests</a> of 1989 and served as president of the People's Republic from 1993 to 2003. His years in power saw rapid market-oriented growth, the return of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macau">Macau</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s entry into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/world-trade-organization">World Trade Organization</a> in 2001.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jiang-zemin.jpg" alt="Jiang Zemin" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Presidential Press and Information Office · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:President_Jiang_Zemin_2002.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The constitution of 1982, collective leadership and retirement norms brought more predictable government under <b>Jiang Zemin</b> and Hu Jintao, but the party kept its monopoly of power, crushing the Tiananmen Square protests on 4 June 1989.</blockquote><a href="/empire/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In October 1997 the Chinese president <b>Jiang Zemin</b>, arriving in Hawaii on a state visit, played it on a Hawaiian lap steel guitar at a dinner with Governor Ben Cayetano, recalling that he had often played it as a student in the 1940s.</blockquote><a href="/songs/aloha-oe">Aloha ʻOe</a></li><li><blockquote>Said to be a favourite of the Communist Party general secretary <b>Jiang Zemin</b>, it was played at his request at the handover of Hong Kong in 1997, and at that of Macau in 1999; it was heard at Party Central Committee meetings and as hold music in provincial…</blockquote><a href="/songs/mo-li-hua">Mo Li Hua</a></li><li><blockquote>At midnight, at a ceremony attended by the Prince of Wales and President <b>Jiang Zemin</b>, sovereignty passed to China after 156 years of British rule.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-30">30 June in history</a></li></ul></section>
